            <div xml:id="d1774">

                <pb facs="1444" n="1328" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1328"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 K77/10.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Costa Rica in Charge of the Legation of
                        Salvador to the Acting Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Salvador</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt, this afternoon, of your esteemed letter dated
                        yesterday<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1774-f1"/> in which you were pleased to
                    inform me that [etc.].</p>
                <p>In answer thereto it affords me great pleasure to say that the Government and
                    people of Salvador appreciate in all its importance the happy thought of His
                    Excellency the President and will receive with the deepest gratification the
                    honor of the visit of his excellency the Secretary of State. I am sure that he
                    will have opportunity to notice how highly they regard the happy and cordial
                    traditional amity which it has been and is the aim of Salvador to cultivate with
                    the United States.</p>
                <p>On Monday, the 12th instant, I called at the Department and left word that I will
                    be very glad if I can be of any service in connection with Secretary Knox’s
                    trip, and I hope to be informed of the precise date when he will arrive in
                    Salvador.</p>
                <p>With many thanks for your courtesy, I am [etc.],</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. B. Calvo.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
